---
/**
 * ACADEMICS → 02 · ACADEMIC STRUCTURE
 *
 * Rebuilt to the client's brief. The previous page opened on a bespoke split
 * hero and put the five stages on a horizontal scroll-snap rail; this one uses
 * the shared banner every other inner page uses and lays the stages out as a
 * connected row, which is what the brief asked for and what a reader comparing
 * five stages actually wants — five things side by side, not five things one
 * flick apart.
 *
 *   Banner        components/ui/PageHero.astro         shared, as Philosophy uses
 *   01            structure/Intro.astro                the overview, and three facts
 *   02            structure/Stages.astro               five cards, chevron-joined
 *   03            structure/Streams.astro              the choice at the end of X
 *   04            structure/Combinations.astro         core + electives per stream
 *
 * ═══ THIS PAGE RUNS A COOL PALETTE, AND ONLY THIS PAGE ══════════════════════
 *
 * The client asked for teal / blue / cyan / indigo / violet washes here instead
 * of the site's warm orange, with orange reserved for CTA buttons. The tokens
 * are therefore declared BELOW, on the page's panel, rather than added to
 * tokens.css — a custom property set on an ancestor inherits into every child
 * component whatever Astro's style scoping does, so the four structure/*
 * components read `--as-*` without importing anything.
 *
 * That containment is the point. The departure is visible in one file, revertible
 * in one file, and cannot leak into the other six Academics pages by accident.
 *
 * ⚠ IT IS STILL A DEPARTURE. Every other page on this site is warm, and a reader
 * moving from Academic Philosophy to Academic Structure crosses a colour
 * boundary. That is a deliberate instruction being followed, not an oversight —
 * but if the section is ever audited for consistency, this is the page that will
 * come up, and this comment is why.
 *
 * ⚠ THE ELECTIVE SUBJECT LISTS ARE PLACEHOLDERS. See the header of
 * structure/Combinations.astro and `streamDetail` in data/academics.ts. The page
 * renders a visible notice for as long as they stay unconfirmed.
 *
 * ⚠ NO <ChapterNav />. The client asked the chapter pager off this page, as they
 * did on Academic Philosophy. It was the only link from here to Teaching &
 * Learning and back to the Academics overview, so this page is now a LEAF: a
 * reader arriving from search leaves via the masthead or the footer. Two of the
 * six Academics pages are now dead ends.
 *
 * ⚠ NO AGES. The school's age criteria live in a Drive-hosted prospectus and are
 * not ours to estimate, so every stage is identified by its class band. Asset
 * request A8.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/ui/PageHero.astro';

import Intro from '../../components/academics/structure/Intro.astro';
import Stages from '../../components/academics/structure/Stages.astro';
import Streams from '../../components/academics/structure/Streams.astro';
import Combinations from '../../components/academics/structure/Combinations.astro';

import banner from '../../assets/photos/sunbeem-3.jpg';
---

<BaseLayout
>
  <PageHero
    src={banner}
  />

  <div class="u-page-panel as-panel">
    <Intro />
    <Stages />
    <Streams />
    <Combinations />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* div.as-panel, not .as-panel: it has to out-specify .u-page-panel in base.css,
     which a bare scoped class only matches rather than beats.

     padding-block: 0 — the four sections carry their own vertical rhythm and the
     panel's default 88/120 would add a band of empty ivory at each end. */
  div.as-panel {
    padding-block: 0;
    background: var(--as-ground);

    /* ── THE COOL PALETTE ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
       Five accents and their washes, plus ink, body text, ground and the two
       shadows the cards share.

       ⚠ THE HUES WERE RE-SPACED AFTER MEASURING THEM. The first set ran
       violet/blue/teal/cyan/indigo and was, in practice, one colour: pairwise
       RGB distance bottomed out at 27 (teal vs cyan) and three more pairs sat
       under 55. Anything under about 40 reads as the same colour. The brief
       asked for "a distinct accent colour" per stage and it was distinct only
       in the stylesheet.

       These five span 150°–290° of hue instead of huddling in the blues, and
       the closest pair is now 64 apart. They are ordered green → violet so the
       five stages read as a progression through the spectrum rather than as
       five unrelated categories.

       ⚠ AND THE WASH CANNOT CARRY IT. A wash is the accent mixed toward white,
       so the distance between two washes is roughly the mix percentage times
       the distance between their accents — at 8% those same five are 5 apart,
       and at 20% they would still be 13. No tint strength fixes this. The
       differentiation therefore lives in SATURATED marks: the filled node on
       the timeline, the class pill's type, the milestone label. The washes stay
       light because their only job is to be a legible ground for accent text.

       Every value measured against white; all five clear AA as small text.

           teal   #0a6d3a  6.6:1      indigo #4340bb  7.8:1
           cyan   #056579  6.6:1      violet #8226c0  7.0:1
           blue   #1259c4  6.4:1 */
    --as-teal: #0a6d3a;
    --as-teal-wash: #e8f2eb;
    --as-cyan: #056579;
    --as-cyan-wash: #e6eff2;
    --as-blue: #1259c4;
    --as-blue-wash: #e8eefa;
    --as-indigo: #4340bb;
    --as-indigo-wash: #ebebf8;
    --as-violet: #8226c0;
    --as-violet-wash: #f3e9f9;

    /* Ink and body copy carry a faint cool cast so type on this page belongs to
       its own palette, without going anywhere near the low-contrast grey-blue
       that a "cool theme" usually degenerates into. Measured on white: 16.4:1
       and 8.9:1. */
    --as-ink: #16182a;
    --as-text: #4a4f63;
    --as-ground: var(--sb-ivory);

    --as-shadow: 0 14px 40px -26px rgba(22, 24, 42, 0.34);
    --as-shadow-hover: 0 28px 64px -28px rgba(22, 24, 42, 0.4);
  }
</style>
